{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: what phrase completes this rule? In translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, _____ is the concept described as: A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls.","Risk constraint"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Implement MCP for every backend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the most capable Claude model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent architecture.\"}]","a","Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions guidance to this case: A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"In a few-shot example.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only in the model's explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model.\"}]","a","Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a translating business problems into Claude-based solutions review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Select the strongest model before clarifying the workload.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.; Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 edge-case review for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: select the TWO recommendations that remain valid. Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on translating business problems into Claude-based solutions? Context: An architect is reviewing translating business problems into Claude-based solutions. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat the word “agent” as a mandatory architecture requirement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip measurable targets until after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.; Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution. Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved end-to-end Claude architecture guidance to this case: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key. Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for end-to-end Claude architecture: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A vector index contains yesterday's account balance. The user asks for the current balance. What should supply the answer?","The authoritative account system/API. Current operational state should come from the system of record. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["System of record — D1.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for end-to-end Claude architecture","The authoritative source for current operational state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Idempotent retry — D1.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for end-to-end Claude architecture","A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
