{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for end-to-end Claude architecture: what phrase completes this rule? In end-to-end Claude architecture, _____ is the concept described as: A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect.","Idempotent retry"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the credit call automatically after any timeout without idempotency.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let Claude issue the credit directly if the prompt says to be cautious.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Store account balance in conversation memory.\"}]","a","Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved end-to-end Claude architecture guidance to this case: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the prompt is long enough.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether the model is the largest available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the response was friendly.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key.\"}]","a","Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a end-to-end Claude architecture review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat vector retrieval as the source of truth for current transactions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.; Keep durable application state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 edge-case review for end-to-end Claude architecture: select the TWO recommendations that remain valid. Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on end-to-end Claude architecture? Context: An architect is reviewing end-to-end Claude architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retry every failed side effect blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Design only the happy path.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep durable application state outside model context.; Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","A deterministic workflow. The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns guidance to this case: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","A bounded agent with dynamic planning. Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? One model call plus retrieval reliably solves a bounded classification task. What should the architect do?","Keep the simple augmented-LLM design unless evaluation shows a need for more orchestration. Complexity should earn measurable value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Workflow — D1.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns","LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Agent — D1.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns","A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: the exact term for “Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.” is {{c1::Workflow}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: the exact term for “Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.” is {{c1::Agent}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
