{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: what phrase completes this rule? In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, _____ is the concept described as: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.","Workflow"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: what phrase completes this rule? In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, _____ is the concept described as: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.","Agent"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An open-ended planner with unrestricted tools.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic workflow.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent swarm.\"}]","a","The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns guidance to this case: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fixed one-step prompt only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A rigid workflow with every path enumerated.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A schema validator alone.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A bounded agent with dynamic planning.\"}]","a","Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a workflow when steps are predictable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an agent whenever a task has more than one step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use a workflow when steps are predictable.; Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.3. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this? Which recommendation should they defend?","Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator. Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved multi-agent orchestration guidance to this case: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts. Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestrator — D1.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for multi-agent orchestration","The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Context isolation — D1.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for multi-agent orchestration","Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: the exact term for “Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.” is {{c1::Orchestrator}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: the exact term for “Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.” is {{c1::Context isolation}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for multi-agent orchestration: what phrase completes this rule? In multi-agent orchestration, _____ is the concept described as: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.","Orchestrator"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for multi-agent orchestration: what phrase completes this rule? In multi-agent orchestration, _____ is the concept described as: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.","Context isolation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A fixed sequential chain even though tasks are independent.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One shared mutable prompt for all workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A worker agent for every sentence.\"}]","a","Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved multi-agent orchestration guidance to this case: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add more workers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove tracing to reduce overhead.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts.\"}]","a","Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a multi-agent orchestration review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Create one agent per trivial step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.; Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","Prompt chaining with validation between stages. Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved decomposing complex problems guidance to this case: Independent searches across four jurisdictions are required. Which pattern best reduces wall-clock time?","Parallelize the independent searches and combine results. Independent work can be parallelized safely. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization — D1.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for decomposing complex problems","Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: the exact term for “Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.” is {{c1::Parallelization}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: the exact term for “Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.” is {{c1::Routing}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for decomposing complex problems: what phrase completes this rule? In decomposing complex problems, _____ is the concept described as: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.","Parallelization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for decomposing complex problems: what phrase completes this rule? In decomposing complex problems, _____ is the concept described as: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.","Routing"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for decomposing complex problems: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No decomposition because multiple calls are always bad.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Prompt chaining with validation between stages.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Unbounded multi-agent exploration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallel execution of all stages.\"}]","a","Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a decomposing complex problems review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Decompose when stages need different context or tools.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Split work by organizational chart instead of information boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Decompose when stages need different context or tools.; Validate useful intermediate outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide? Which recommendation should they defend?","Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone. Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved aligning architecture to business value guidance to this case: A team reports 95% model accuracy but cannot say whether customer resolution time improved. What is missing?","A link between technical performance and a business outcome/baseline. Technical metrics must connect to value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Technical metric — D1.6 application — P2 synthesis lens for aligning architecture to business value","A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: the exact term for “Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.” is {{c1::Technical metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: the exact term for “Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.” is {{c1::Business metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for aligning architecture to business value: what phrase completes this rule? In aligning architecture to business value, _____ is the concept described as: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.","Technical metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for aligning architecture to business value: what phrase completes this rule? In aligning architecture to business value, _____ is the concept described as: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.","Business metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore human-review cost because it is not AI spend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always choose the cheaper model call.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always choose the higher-capability model.\"}]","a","Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a aligning architecture to business value review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support aligning architecture to business value?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat human review as free.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a baseline before claiming improvement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize token cost even when task success drops.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define a baseline before claiming improvement.; Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.6. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound discovery-to-architecture flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the business outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Quantify success and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Separate model vs deterministic responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the simplest viable architecture\"}]","The architecture follows the outcome and constraints, not the reverse. Sequence reinforcement for D1.1. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for end-to-end Claude architecture: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a typical protected request path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the caller\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate input and gather context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run model/tool work\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic verification\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute output/action and record telemetry\"}]","Identity and validation precede model/tool work; protected execution follows verification. Sequence reinforcement for D1.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sensible architecture-escalation strategy.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Test a simple augmented model call\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Add a workflow if predictable stages are needed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Use a bounded agent if dynamic planning is required\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Add multi-agent complexity only when evaluation justifies it\"}]","Start simple and escalate only when measured requirements demand it. Sequence reinforcement for D1.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for multi-agent orchestration: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order the orchestrator-worker pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Interpret the overall goal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Decompose into bounded subtasks\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Delegate work to workers\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect and validate results\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Synthesize the final result\"}]","The orchestrator plans, delegates, validates, then synthesizes. Sequence reinforcement for D1.4. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for decomposing complex problems: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a prompt-chaining workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Run the first bounded stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate its intermediate output\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Pass the validated result to the next stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Produce and verify the final output\"}]","Dependent stages execute in order with validation at useful boundaries. Sequence reinforcement for D1.5. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice? Which recommendation should they defend?","Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model. Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved Claude model selection guidance to this case: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation. Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for Claude model selection: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A workflow has easy classification cases and rare complex exceptions. What design may improve economics if validated?","Route routine cases to a fast model and difficult cases to a stronger model. Evaluated routing can match model capability to workload difficulty. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active model — D2.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for Claude model selection","A fully supported model recommended for current use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Deprecated model — D2.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for Claude model selection","A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A fully supported model recommended for current use.” is {{c1::Active model}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.” is {{c1::Deprecated model}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved Claude model selection rule? Choose the model that meets the workload's _____ at acceptable latency and cost.” is {{c1::quality threshold}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for Claude model selection: what phrase completes this rule? In Claude model selection, _____ is the concept described as: A fully supported model recommended for current use.","Active model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for Claude model selection: what phrase completes this rule? In Claude model selection, _____ is the concept described as: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.","Deprecated model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for Claude model selection: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route randomly between models.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always use the strongest model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always use the cheapest model even if it fails quality.\"}]","a","Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved Claude model selection guidance to this case: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newer model is behaviorally identical.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only compare benchmark scores.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change the model without testing because the API shape is similar.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation.\"}]","a","Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a Claude model selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate models on the actual workload.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newest model is always best.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate models on the actual workload.; Re-run regressions after model changes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation? Which recommendation should they defend?","Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic. Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails guidance to this case: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently. Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Downstream software requires valid structured output. What should the architecture add?","An explicit output contract plus schema validation. Structure should be specified and validated when machines depend on it. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Behavioral instruction — D2.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for system prompts, templates, and guardrails","Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Enforceable control — D2.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for system prompts, templates, and guardrails","Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.” is {{c1::Behavioral instruction}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.” is {{c1::Enforceable control}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails rule? Use prompts to guide behavior; use _____ to enforce hard security and policy invariants.” is {{c1::deterministic controls}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: what phrase completes this rule? In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, _____ is the concept described as: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.","Behavioral instruction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: what phrase completes this rule? In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, _____ is the concept described as: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.","Enforceable control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to self-check twice.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put the rule only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a longer example showing a $499 refund.\"}]","a","Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails guidance to this case: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Concatenate all text into one unstructured prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell retrieved text it is trusted.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely on the model to always ignore injections.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently.\"}]","a","Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a system prompts, templates, and guardrails review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use clear trusted instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat a system prompt as an access-control list.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use clear trusted instructions.; Separate untrusted content from policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step? Which recommendation should they defend?","Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate. Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved prompt engineering techniques guidance to this case: A straightforward extraction task already meets its quality target zero-shot. What should the team do?","Keep the simpler prompt unless evaluation identifies a failure. Use the lightest technique that passes the evaluation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Zero-shot — D2.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt engineering techniques","Clear direct instructions without worked examples."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Few-shot / multishot — D2.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt engineering techniques","Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: the exact term for “Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.” is {{c1::Zero-shot}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: the exact term for “Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.” is {{c1::Few-shot / multishot}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt engineering techniques: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt engineering techniques, _____ is the concept described as: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.","Zero-shot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt engineering techniques: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt engineering techniques, _____ is the concept described as: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.","Few-shot / multishot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide the labels from the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add dozens of irrelevant examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Switch to an agent immediately.\"}]","a","Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a prompt engineering techniques review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Start with clear direct instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Force visible step-by-step reasoning for every task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Start with clear direct instructions.; Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.3. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change? Which recommendation should they defend?","Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus. JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved context-window and token management guidance to this case: A long-running agent approaches practical context limits. What should compaction preserve?","Key decisions, constraints, unresolved work, and important evidence. Compaction reduces size while preserving decision-critical information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active context — D2.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for context-window and token management","Information currently visible to the model for the present inference."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: the exact term for “Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.” is {{c1::Active context}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: the exact term for “Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.” is {{c1::Compaction}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for context-window and token management: what phrase completes this rule? In context-window and token management, _____ is the concept described as: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.","Active context"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for context-window and token management: what phrase completes this rule? In context-window and token management, _____ is the concept described as: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.","Compaction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for context-window and token management: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always use multiple agents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt verbosity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the corpus in conversation history.\"}]","a","JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a context-window and token management review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support context-window and token management?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume larger windows eliminate relevance problems.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Preload every available document.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.; Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization? Which recommendation should they defend?","Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately. Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills guidance to this case: A shared Skill changes how production agents perform a regulated workflow. How should it be managed?","Version, review, test, and control changes like other operational assets. Reusable agent instructions/resources can change behavior and should be governed. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt template — D2.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills","Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: the exact term for “Within prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, what term matches this definition: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.” is {{c1::Prompt template}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills rule? Reuse is safest when the content is _____ that freshness is not compromised.” is {{c1::stable enough}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, _____ is the concept described as: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.","Prompt template"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove freshness checks from current data.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache each client's live case status indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the manual into every variable section.\"}]","a","Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a prompt reuse, caching, and Skills review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt reuse, caching, and Skills?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one giant reusable prompt for unrelated workloads.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse stable expensive context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache rapidly changing business state indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reuse stable expensive context.; Keep volatile state fresh.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for Claude model selection: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation. Sequence reinforcement for D2.1. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a secure prompt-to-action pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted system instructions\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Insert user/retrieved content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an output/action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Validate schema and authorization deterministically\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only if controls pass\"}]","Behavioral prompting precedes deterministic validation and execution. Sequence reinforcement for D2.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for prompt engineering techniques: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an evidence-driven prompt-improvement loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish a simple baseline prompt\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluations\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify a specific failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply the lightest targeted prompting change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-run evaluation and regression checks\"}]","Prompt complexity should be added in response to observed failures. Sequence reinforcement for D2.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for Claude model selection: place these steps in the order you would defend. Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks. Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved tool and agent capability bloat guidance to this case: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions. General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for tool and agent capability bloat: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An agent has twelve overlapping CRM tools with vague names and often chooses the wrong one. What is the best improvement?","Reduce overlap and define clearer, distinct tool boundaries and descriptions. Overlapping capability increases selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability bloat — D3.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for tool and agent capability bloat","Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Least privilege — D3.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for tool and agent capability bloat","Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.” is {{c1::Capability bloat}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.” is {{c1::Least privilege}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved tool and agent capability bloat rule? More exposed capability increases the potential _____ if an agent is compromised or behaves incorrectly.” is {{c1::blast radius}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for tool and agent capability bloat: what phrase completes this rule? In tool and agent capability bloat, _____ is the concept described as: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.","Capability bloat"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for tool and agent capability bloat: what phrase completes this rule? In tool and agent capability bloat, _____ is the concept described as: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.","Least privilege"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add more unrelated tools so selection is balanced.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logging but keep admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell the model never to misuse the credential.\"}]","a","Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved tool and agent capability bloat guidance to this case: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ban all broad tools regardless of task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give unrestricted production shell access.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on a system prompt to protect the host.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions.\"}]","a","General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a tool and agent capability bloat review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Expose only tools required for the task.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every agent a shared admin credential.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Expose only tools required for the task.; Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do? Which recommendation should they defend?","Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy. Prompt text is not authentication. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved authentication and authorization guidance to this case: An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context. Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authentication — D3.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for authentication and authorization","Establishing the identity of the caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authorization — D3.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for authentication and authorization","Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for authentication and authorization: the exact term for “Within authentication and authorization, what term matches this definition: Establishing the identity of the caller.” is {{c1::Authentication}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
